        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                "word": "épistémologie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "578b321d-cd44-4fde-93b7-efa530db4550",
                        "entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "épistémologies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                        "entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Partie de la philosophie qui étudie l’histoire, les méthodes, les principes des sciences."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3004e388-55c4-4514-a4b7-6da6f93ee357",
                                "sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                                "text": "Il semble au contraire que, dans l’épistémologie de la physique épicurienne, l’observation du monde, sa connaissance empirique, soit non seulement légitime, mais encore nécessaire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3df9149b-056b-4ff5-b4b7-54bd71d8ec79",
                                "sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                                "text": "Nul ne saurait nier qu’une certaine inculture scientifique est devenue intellectuellement et socialement problématique : elle empêche de fonder une épistémologie rigoureuse de la science contemporaine, favorise l’emprise des gourous de toutes sortes et rend délicate l’organisation de débats sérieux sur l’usage que nous voulons faire des technologies"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "373475e2-2b4b-4a9a-8bde-64de3f9beff0",
                        "source_entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Epistemologie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Epistemologie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "251f4393-e50b-3cc7-ae5d-c0626c5df7be",
                                        "entry_id": "64fcf0f6-fcba-3dbb-863f-cdb21886e335",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lehre der Wissenschaft; Wissenschaftslehre; Erkenntnistheorie"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3206d520-8a98-4e79-a93d-39e5dcfa0a99",
                                                "sense_id": "251f4393-e50b-3cc7-ae5d-c0626c5df7be",
                                                "text": "Seit den 1930er Jahren hat sich die Epistemologie in Frankreich als eine Richtung der gegenwärtigen Philosophie konstituiert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "808eef15-0b4a-4eaf-8d87-6e52bad234e4",
                                                "sense_id": "251f4393-e50b-3cc7-ae5d-c0626c5df7be",
                                                "text": "„Die scholastische Epistemologie stellt sowohl die Mehrdeutigkeit wie die divergierenden Verwendungsweisen des Terminus Wissen von Anfang an in Rechnung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1fdf9f8-6f7a-4a61-bd16-7725fda7e8bc",
                                                "sense_id": "251f4393-e50b-3cc7-ae5d-c0626c5df7be",
                                                "text": "„Schopenhauers Philosophie ist zuvorderst ein Kommentar zu den Voraussetzungen der Erkenntnis, eine Epistemologie.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d11e5c6a-e55a-4cf6-b244-db798e4338c6",
                        "source_entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Erkenntnistheorie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Erkenntnistheorie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edd48461-a73a-3e55-824b-c0f59a548731",
                                        "entry_id": "ca35cbf6-bd9b-3059-831c-6806e9a3b97d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "derjenige Zweig der Philosophie, der die objektive Geltung menschlichen Erkennens, seine Reichweite und Grenzen untersucht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77767fdc-153b-4350-97f5-1d721e232315",
                                                "sense_id": "edd48461-a73a-3e55-824b-c0f59a548731",
                                                "text": "Die Erkenntnistheorie sichert die Wahrheitsbefähigung unseres Geistes, der das Seiende erfassen kann."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b2a96cc-1c64-4481-a773-068aee12df9f",
                                                "sense_id": "edd48461-a73a-3e55-824b-c0f59a548731",
                                                "text": "„Die Erkenntnistheorie bereitet für Einstein die physikalische Arbeit vor.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8e6939df-1d4d-4a8f-861f-b52b383911c4",
                        "source_entry_id": "633c1815-1876-3deb-92d0-ac5feb9a8151",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bff8410-9197-3bc8-b7c2-87980a2c8ea1",
                        "target_lang_word": "epistemology",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "epistemology",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a6f2a34-67e8-33d9-beea-44508f4d6002",
                                        "entry_id": "d6b0e5ce-b8de-3475-8ee8-3d97118482bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The branch of philosophy dealing with the study of knowledge; the theory of knowledge, asking such questions as \\\"What is knowledge?\\\", \\\"How is knowledge acquired?\\\", \\\"What do people know?\\\", \\\"How do we know what we know?\\\", \\\"How do we know it is true?\\\", and so on."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c537572f-b9b6-4f2d-b0d4-930fef66e5ab",
                                                "sense_id": "4a6f2a34-67e8-33d9-beea-44508f4d6002",
                                                "text": "Some thinkers take the view that, beginning with the work of Descartes, epistemology began to replace metaphysics as the most important area of philosophy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7108e88-a2fe-492d-aaf8-e05a355544a8",
                                                "sense_id": "4a6f2a34-67e8-33d9-beea-44508f4d6002",
                                                "text": "[P]hilosophers of the time [early 20th century] were primarily concerned with epistemology and the foundations of the sciences; they often spoke as if we were separated from the real world by a screen of \"representations\" or \"sense-data\"; they tended to regard our approach to the world as one of disinterested observation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85dc285c-d6c4-3946-93d6-679f526455b7",
                                        "entry_id": "d6b0e5ce-b8de-3475-8ee8-3d97118482bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particular instance, version, or school thereof; a particular theory of knowledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dbe7f27-a048-4393-8303-9a96389733e8",
                                                "sense_id": "85dc285c-d6c4-3946-93d6-679f526455b7",
                                                "text": "In his epistemology, Plato maintains that our knowledge of universal concepts is a kind of recollection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "311c48f7-e716-495f-8ebf-8c5713049000",
                                                "sense_id": "85dc285c-d6c4-3946-93d6-679f526455b7",
                                                "text": "I believe that 'intuitionism' is usually, and rightly, taken to mean Brouwer's epistemology of mathematics, which is unrelated to the origin or content of topos theory."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
